From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: keep capture START successful when the microphone
 is slow or missing

A game that opens voice chat starts the capture stream. When the Mac input
device took longer than 200 ms to start, PCM_START failed with IO_ERR and the
late start was canceled. PipeWire retried snd_pcm_start in a tight loop at
real-time priority, the guest killed it with SIGKILL, and the game lost all
sound for the rest of the session.

Let a slow start finish in the background and answer START with OK. A start
that fails (no input device, permission denied) is logged. While no input
arrives, including while a start stuck in HAL holds the stream, the pump
completes the guest's reads with silence at the stream's rate: a read that
never completes fails in the guest with EIO, and the watchdog would fail it
with IO_ERR. Real input takes over once the device delivers. Playback is not
affected. The start command queue no longer refuses a request while another
one is pending.
---
